    "narrative": "The Austin Waves prioritize speed today, highlighted by **Nasim Nunez** earning our highest efficiency score of 62.09. Facing a vulnerable 5.10 xERA from Feltner, **Nasim Nunez** is a primary target despite the #9 spot in the order; his elite sprint speed makes him the optimal engine for our stolen base strategy, and the favorable matchup against a struggling right-hander elevates his floor significantly. **Sam Antonacci** follows closely at 59.34, benefiting from a prime #1 lineup slot against Rocker. His high-volume opportunity at the top of the order creates a solid foundation, with his platoon advantage over the right-handed Rocker providing the necessary buffer to push him past our marginal threshold.\n\nWhile **Tommy White** (55.05), **Miguel Vargas** (54.64), and **Jackson Merrill** (51.55) provide steady output, they inhabit the \"Marginal\" zone. **Jackson Merrill** faces the toughest matchup of the day against Ashcraft, whose 3.28 xERA forces a downward adjustment in our scoring model, though **Jackson Merrill** remains a start due to his dynamic platoon profile and consistent run-scoring potential. The closest bench decision was centered on balancing the raw power of **Tommy White** against the risk of lineup uncertainty; we are currently projecting him in the #5 spot, but should the official card show him lower, his utility score is volatile. With **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** all sidelined by off-days, our bench is strictly defensive today, leaving little room for error if weather-related delays emerge at these specific venues. We are locked into this configuration to maximize our stolen base potential and mitigate the high-xERA threats presented by the daily slate.",
